  "body": "Reported twice as *\"analytics resets after 50,070 requests\"*. Checked against the reporter's live server:\n\n```\nwindowed total     : 50,080     <- oscillates 50,000 -> 50,099 -> back\nretained_rows_max  : 50,000\nretention notice   : SHOWN\nlifetime requests  : 50,620     <- climbing correctly\ncompressed bodies  :    573     <- 4.46.0 running\n```\n\nNothing resets, and nothing was broken. Prune runs every 100 inserts, so stored rows climb just past the cap and drop back to it, forever. **A card labelled \"Total requests\" made that look like a counter resetting.**\n\n## The label was the bug\n\n- **\"Total requests\" → \"Stored requests\"**, with `at the storage cap — older ones deleted` underneath once the cap is reached. The number was always right for what it counted; the label promised something it could not deliver.\n- The retention note now leads with the consequence nobody had stated: **pruned requests are deleted**. They cannot be listed, opened or searched. All-time keeps counting, but those are *counts* — a rollup does not bring rows back. Raising `REQUEST_LOG_MAX_ROWS` is the only way to browse further back, and the note now quotes the real cost (~7 KB a request compressed, against 41 KB before) so the disk trade is concrete rather than abstract.\n- Page size gains **250** and **500**, matching the limit the API already allowed.\n\n## Verification\n\nTwo tests pin that the dashboard hides nothing of what is stored: paging reaches every row, and the largest page size the UI offers is accepted. Local suite 3,407 passed, with the 6 known PowerShell installer failures that predate this branch.\n\nPATCH: 4.46.0 → 4.46.1.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
